+### Should I run ASO on a specific node pool in AKS?
+
+ASO doesn't set any AKS-specific node affinity by default, because ASO is supported on many kinds of Kubernetes
+clusters, not just AKS. If you want to keep ASO off your user node pools (or on your system node pool), you can
+configure this yourself with a `preferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution` node affinity in the Helm values.
+For example, to prefer scheduling on AKS system node pools:
+
+```yaml
+affinity:
+  nodeAffinity:
+    preferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
+    - weight: 100
+      preference:
+        matchExpressions:
+        - key: kubernetes.azure.com/mode
+          operator: In
+          values:
+          - system
+```
+
+Using `preferred` rather than `required` keeps ASO schedulable on clusters that don't have this label.
+
