+### How do I install ASO with Argo CD?
+
+Point Argo CD at the ASO Helm chart repository rather than at the chart source directory in the git repository.
+For example:
+
+```yaml
+  source:
+    repoURL: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure/azure-service-operator/main/v2/charts
+    targetRevision: v2.8.0
+    chart: azure-service-operator
+    helm:
+```
+
+Using the git source directory instead will miss generated templates such as the
+`azureserviceoperator-manager-role` ClusterRole, and the ASO pod will fail to start. See
+[Installing with Argo CD]({{< relref "installing-from-helm#installing-with-argo-cd" >}}) for details.
+
+### How do I pass data between ASO resources?
+
+ASO resources can reference each other directly, so you usually don't need to copy values around by hand.
+Use the `operatorSpec` of a resource to export values (such as an ID, endpoint, or key) into a ConfigMap or
+Secret, and then reference those values from other resources. See
+[ConfigMaps]({{< relref "configmaps" >}}) and [Secrets]({{< relref "secrets" >}}) for details.
+
 ### What's the difference between ASO and Crossplane.io?
 
 There are a lot of similarities between ASO and Crossplane. They do similar things and have similar audiences. You can see some of this discussed [here](https://github.com/Azure/azure-service-operator/issues/1190).
