+ASO with Helm.
+
+## Installing with Argo CD
+
+When installing ASO with [Argo CD](https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/), make sure to point Argo CD at the
+Helm chart repository rather than at the chart source directory in the ASO git repository. Argo CD renders the
+chart from the repository (the packaged `.tgz`), which includes all generated templates such as the
+`azureserviceoperator-manager-role` ClusterRole. Pointing Argo CD at the `v2/charts/azure-service-operator`
+directory in the git repository instead will miss those generated templates, and the ASO pod will fail to start.
+
+An example Argo CD `Application`:
+
+```yaml
+apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
+kind: Application
+spec:
+  source:
+    repoURL: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure/azure-service-operator/main/v2/charts
+    targetRevision: v2.8.0
+    chart: azure-service-operator
+    helm:
+      releaseName: aso2
+      valuesObject:
+        installCRDs: true
+        crdPattern: 'containerregistry.azure.com/*'
+```
+
+Note that the Helm chart for a given release is published to the chart repository shortly _after_ the release
+tag is created, so the chart version may not exist in the repository at the exact moment the tag is cut.
